# collections_fase1b.tkr — the fase1b generic keyed/ordered collections end-to-end host.
# A SELF-CONTAINED project (its own copy of the IEq/IOrd/IHash capability corpus + StrKey/I64Key
# conformers + the Dictionary/HashSet/SortedSet/PriorityQueue/SortedDictionary bodies), because the
# stdlib's teko::cmp/teko::collections are compiler-internal and not visible to a user project — the
# capability_iface precedent. Each scenario instantiates its collection at TWO widths and asserts its
# announced behavior, so a monomorph/dispatch relapse names itself. Runs on the C backend.

Feature: collections_fase1b — generic keyed & ordered collections on the 9-ops + #254 capability model

  Scenario: ihash_consistency — G1 hash-eq consistency on StrKey/I64Key (equal payload → equal hash + __eq)
    When built and run
    Then stdout pattern = "scenario ihash_consistency: ok"

  Scenario: combinators_edges — G2a arr_insert_at/swap/reverse/slice edge cases
    When built and run
    Then stdout pattern = "scenario combinators_edges: ok"

  Scenario: dictionary_roundtrip — G3 Dictionary<StrKey,i64> + <I64Key,str> insert/update/get/remove
    When built and run
    Then stdout pattern = "scenario dictionary_roundtrip: ok"

  Scenario: hashset_membership — G4 HashSet<StrKey> + <I64Key> add/contains/remove, idempotent add
    When built and run
    Then stdout pattern = "scenario hashset_membership: ok"

  Scenario: sortedset_ordering — G5 SortedSet<I64Key> + <StrKey> out-of-order inserts emerge sorted
    When built and run
    Then stdout pattern = "scenario sortedset_ordering: ok"

  Scenario: priorityqueue_ordering — G5 PriorityQueue<I64Key> dequeues min-first, <StrKey> peeks min
    When built and run
    Then stdout pattern = "scenario priorityqueue_ordering: ok"

  Scenario: sorteddict_ordering — G5 SortedDictionary<I64Key,str> + <StrKey,i64> keeps keys ascending
    When built and run
    Then stdout pattern = "scenario sorteddict_ordering: ok"
